**H&E only; ignore special-stain quality issues.** Quality issues for OTHER stains (Gram, GMS, PAS, Trichrome, Iron, IHC) are NOT in scope and must NOT trigger `out_of_focus` / `inadequate_for_dx` / `not_performed` flags. The MORPHOLOGICAL RESULT of a special stain IS in scope (e.g. "GMS positive for fungal organisms" → `fungal` finding).

# Output format

Return a single JSON object (no comments, no extra keys, no text outside the JSON):

```
{
  "case_id": "<the case_id below>",
  "findings": [
    {
      "organ": "<one of the organs>",
      "text_source": "<one of: site_report, cpl_review_of_scans, cpl_slides, implicit_cpl>",
      "condition": "<schema condition name>",
      "severity": "<schema severity value or null>",
      "extent": "<schema extent value or null>",
      "modifiers": { "<modifier_key>": "<schema-allowed value>" },
      "supporting_quote": "<verbatim phrase ≤120 chars>",
      "negated": false
    }
  ],
  "negations": [
    { "organ": "<organ>", "text_source": "<text_source>", "negation_group": "<negation_group>", "supporting_quote": "<verbatim>" }
  ],
  "quality_flags": [
    { "organ": "<organ>", "text_source": "<text_source>", "flag": "<flag>", "severity": null, "extent": null, "modifiers": {}, "supporting_quote": "<verbatim>" }
  ],
  "uncertain": [
    { "organ": "<organ>", "text_source": "<text_source>", "condition": "<schema condition name>", "reason": "<one of: hedge, syndrome_substrate_ambiguous, pathologist_uncertainty>", "supporting_quote": "<verbatim>" }
  ]
}
```

`modifiers` may be `{}`. `uncertain` may be `[]` (most cases have none). **Strict deduplication**: at most ONE record per `(organ, text_source, condition|negation_group|flag)` key.

The `uncertain[]` array records cases where the pathologist hedged a specific morphology; see Principle 13. An uncertain entry signals "neither emit as positive in `findings[]` NOR leave as a clean negative". Downstream training will NaN-mask the affected (case, organ, condition) label.

